  "citizens_rate_source_date": null,
  "citizens_temporal_note": "Citizens rates move on the statutory glide path. Per Citizens' 2025 Rate Kit, the Miami-Dade HO-3 book-average premium rose +13.5% ($5,113 \u2192 $5,804), effective ~June 2025 (statewide HO-3 +13.5%). The 2026 filing (effective 6/1/2026) proposes -0.8% after glide-path capping, with the indicated actuarially-sound premium down 43% on SB 2-A reinsurance savings. The CHOICES figures here may reflect a filing generation behind the live rate; the API does not expose the rate-effective date (see citizens_rate_source_date).",
  "rate_currency_note": "Every premium in this file is a most-recent-OIR-approved FILED rate for a fixed CHOICES model home, as of an effective date the CHOICES API does not disclose; last_verified is the FETCH date, not the rate-effective date. Writer-v2 must cite these as 'illustrative filed rates' (never as current market quotes), always paired with last_verified and the illustrative_caveat. This applies to every carrier, not just Citizens."
